'''Guarapiranga''' ({{Literal translation|place of the reddish wood}}) is one of ten regions of [[Hesperia]], within the [[Baliscan Confederation]]. It is bordered by [[Las Serras]] to the north, the [[Aethiopian Ocean|Aethiopic Ocean]] to the east, [[Piemont]] to the south, and [[Campostella]] to the southwest, and [[Trás-as-Montanyas Sur]] to the west. It has an area of {{convert|53606.93|km2|abbr=on}} making it the 10th-largest region of Balisca. It was determined to have a population of 1,627,288 in the [[2025 Baliscan census|2025 census]]. The capital of Guarapiranga is [[Sant Marc]], and largest city is [[Guadalajara]].

